      "text": "To determine the month in which Hal changes the batteries for the 25th time, we need to account for the fact that the first change occurred in May and each subsequent change happens every 5 months. \n\n1. Identify the interval of months between each change: 5 months.\n2. Determine how many full intervals of 5 months fit into 25 changes: \n   \\[\n   \\frac{25 \\text{ changes}}{5 \\text{ months/interval}} = 5 \\text{ intervals}\n   \\]\n3. Calculate the total number of months elapsed after 5 intervals:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ intervals} \\times 5 \\text{ months/interval} = 25 \\text{ months}\n   \\]\n4. Add these 25 months to the initial month (May):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Initial month (May) plus 25 months} = \\text{May} + 25 \\text{ months}\n   \\]\n\nTo convert 25 months into years and months:\n   \\[\n   25 \\text{ months} = 2 \\text{ years and } 1 \\text{ month}\n   \\]\n   Because 1 year has 12 months:\n   \\[\n   25 \\text{ months} = 2 \\text{ years} + 1 \\text{ month}\n   \\]\n\nNow add this duration to May:\n   \\[\n   \\text{May + 2 years and 1 month} = \\text{May + December}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, 25 months after May is December.\n\nThus, the month in which Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time is \\(\\boxed{\\text{December}}\\).",
