      "text": "To determine the month in which Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time, we need to calculate the total elapsed time in years and then convert it to the corresponding month.\n\n1. **Determine the intervals between changes:**\n   - Since Hal changes the batteries every 5 months, the intervals between the changes are also 5 months.\n\n2. **Calculate the total time elapsed in years:**\n   - There are 12 months in a year.\n   - The time elapsed after \\( n \\) changes is \\( 5n \\) months.\n   - We need to find the time elapsed for the 25th change, so:\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 25 = 125 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Convert the total months to years:**\n   - There are 12 months in a year, so:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{125}{12} \\approx 10.4167 \\text{ years}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Identify the month of the 11th year:**\n   - Since the first change was in May, we need to find the month of the 11th year.\n   - The calendar progression from May to the 11th year will involve:\n     - Adding 10 years (10 years from May)\n     - August changes because 10 years in the calendar for May repeats every 12 years in 11 cases.\n   - Therefore, the 11th year from May will be:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Year value} = 2022 - 10 = 2012 \\text{ (since the year is not a leap year, the month is mid-August)}\n     \\]\n   - The month in 2012 is August.\n\nThus, the batteries will be changed for the 25th time in \\(\\boxed{\\text{August}}\\).",
